course: dictionary
lesson: 511
title: Assess: judging how good or big something is
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To assess something means to judge it carefully, deciding how good, big, important or serious it is. Teachers assess work, and you can assess your own learning too.
explain: «Year 6 writing in England is assessed by the teacher from work across the year; there is no single writing exam.» Assessed here means the teacher judges the writing from work over the whole year, not from one test on one day.
explain: Assess can also mean working out the amount or value of something. Before you act, you might assess the risk, deciding how dangerous something is. Clue words to look for are judge, decide, work out, how good and how serious.
fact: Assess is a verb: assess, assesses, assessed, assessing.
fact: «Assess» means to judge how good, big, important or serious something is.
fact: «Assess» can also mean to work out the amount or value of something.
fact: Common phrases: assess the damage, risk assessment, self-assess, be assessed on.
fact: «Year 6 writing in England is assessed by the teacher from work across the year; there is no single writing exam.»
exercise: The teacher will assess your story to decide how good it is. What does assess mean here? | Throw it away | Read it aloud to the class | Copy it neatly | *Judge how good it is
exercise: After the storm, the builder must assess the damage before fixing the roof. What is the builder doing? | Going home early | *Working out how bad the damage is | Painting the roof | Ordering a new house
exercise: Which word in «Year 6 writing in England is assessed by the teacher» is another form of assess? | teacher | Year | England | *assessed
test: Which word means the same as assess when you decide how big or serious something is? | Copy | Ignore | Forget | *Judge
test: Mia says, «I will self-assess my maths.» What does she plan to do? | Ask her teacher to do her maths for her | Hide her maths book | Stop doing maths | *Judge her own maths learning
exam: Which sentence uses assess to mean work out an amount or value? | We played football at break | The bus was late again | The cat slept all day | *The shopkeeper must assess the value of the old painting
